The WAAM process involves complex multi-physics phenomena that must be accurately represented within the DT framework to enable reliable prediction and support adaptive control. The primary physical aspects include the transfer of heat from the heating source (electric arc) to the substrate and deposited layers, solidification and phase transformations during cooling and the development of residual stresses and strains. Thermal modeling is fundamentally important, as the WAAM process is dominated by transient heat conduction with localized heat input from the electric arc. The governing equation of transient heat conduction was expressed as: 1 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
